ven-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Arpin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Weller</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ezrin-dependent promotion of glioma cell clonogenicity, motility, and invasion mediated by BCL-2 and transforming growth factor-<italic>&#x003b2;</italic><sub>2</sub></article-title><source><italic>The Journal of Neuroscience</italic></source><year>2001</year><volume>21</volume><issue>10</issue><fpage>3360</fpage><lpage>3368</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11331365</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Uhl</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Aulwurm</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wischhusen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>SD-208, a novel transforming growth factor <italic>&#x003b2;</italic> receptor I kinase inhibitor, inhibits growth and invasiveness and enhances immunogenicity of murine and human glioma cells in vitro and in vivo</article-title><source><italic>Cancer Research</italic></source><year>2004</year><volume>64</volume><issue>21</issue><fpage>7954</fpage><lpage>7961</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15520202</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Friese</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Wischhusen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Wick</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>RNA interference targeting transforming growth factor-<italic>&#x003b2;</italic> enhances NKG2D-mediated antiglioma immune response, inhibits glioma cell migration and invasiveness, and abrogates tumorigenicity in vivo</article-title><source><italic>Cancer Research</italic></source><year>2004</